drift.rs is the ground truth for the drift engine's behavior — how the `links-reviewed:` epoch selects its certification commit, what classifies a link healthy/uncertified/broken/drifted/moved/unverifiable, and which outcomes `--fix` relocates versus skips. drift_relocation.rs pins that contract's relocation tiers and remedy texts as in-suite witness controls, so a change to the classification or skip semantics must keep them green; the fragment-links-and-coverage, resolving-skipped-fixes, and running-wiki-check sections describe that behavior for operators, so a change must also be re-verified against all three descriptions, and a doc that re-describes the contract must stay true of the implementation and of what the pins exercise.
